{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>If to call you.</b> To invite you to eat with them at the sacrifice of peace offerings — <b>go with them.</b> And if you ask: what changed in the matter, that now He said to him 'go with them' but at first He said to him 'you shall not go with them'? One may answer: at first He said only 'you shall not go with them to curse them.' Another interpretation: this is no change — after he added and sent other messengers, many and more distinguished than the first ones. Another interpretation: <b>if to call you</b> — if they are such fools that they came to call you a second time after I said to you 'you shall not go with them,' <b>arise, go with them</b> — and let them see that it will avail them nothing."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:17.713324540Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}